spec contract_check 2026-01-01
"""
Whether a landlord's contract may be signed as offered, checked against what
the listing advertised and the platform's own limit on a deposit.
Fictional demonstration policy for the HousingAnywhere journey prototype.
Illustrative only: it does not describe HousingAnywhere policy or Dutch law.
"""

uses lemma units

data money: measure
  -> unit eur: 1.00
  -> decimals 2
  -> minimum 0 eur

data advertised_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What monthly rent did the listing advertise?"

data contract_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What monthly rent does the contract state?"

data contract_service_charge: money
  -> help "What recurring service charge does the contract add on top of the rent?"
  -> suggest 0 eur

data advertised_deposit: money
  -> help "What deposit did the listing advertise?"

data contract_deposit: money
  -> help "What deposit does the contract require?"

data contract_notice_period: units.calendar
  -> help "How much notice does the contract require before the tenant may leave?"


rule contract_monthly_cost:
  contract_monthly_rent + contract_service_charge

rule undisclosed_monthly_cost:
  contract_monthly_cost - advertised_monthly_rent

rule maximum_deposit:
  2 * advertised_monthly_rent

rule monthly_cost_as_advertised:
  contract_monthly_cost <= advertised_monthly_rent

rule deposit_as_advertised:
  contract_deposit <= advertised_deposit

rule deposit_within_cap:
  contract_deposit <= maximum_deposit

rule notice_period_acceptable:
  contract_notice_period <= 1 month

rule contract_may_be_signed:
  monthly_cost_as_advertised and deposit_as_advertised
  and deposit_within_cap
  and notice_period_acceptable


spec deposit_settlement 2026-01-01
"""
What may be withheld from a deposit at the end of a tenancy, and what must be
returned. A deduction needs evidence from both the move-in and the move-out
record, and normal wear is never chargeable.
Fictional demonstration policy for the HousingAnywhere journey prototype.
Illustrative only: it does not describe HousingAnywhere policy or Dutch law.
"""

data money: measure
  -> unit eur: 1.00
  -> decimals 2
  -> minimum 0 eur

data deposit_held: money
  -> help "How much deposit is being held?"

data rent_arrears: money
  -> help "How much unpaid rent is still outstanding?"
  -> suggest 0 eur

data claimed_amount: money
  -> help "How much is the landlord claiming for the condition of the home?"

data claim_category: text
  -> option "none"
  -> option "normal_wear"
  -> option "accidental_damage"
  -> option "cleaning"
  -> option "missing_item"
  -> option "redecoration"
  -> help "What kind of claim is the landlord making?"

data claim_evidenced: boolean
  -> help "Is there both move-in and move-out evidence for this claim?"
  -> suggest false


rule chargeable_claim:
  veto "This kind of claim is not priced in the settlement policy"
  unless claim_category is "none"
    then 0 eur
  unless claim_category is "normal_wear"
    then 0 eur
  unless claim_category is "accidental_damage"
    then claimed_amount
  unless claim_category is "cleaning"
    then claimed_amount
  unless claim_category is "missing_item"
    then claimed_amount

rule evidenced_claim:
  chargeable_claim
  unless claim_evidenced is false then 0 eur

rule total_claimed:
  rent_arrears + claimed_amount

rule total_deduction:
  rent_arrears + evidenced_claim

rule deduction_payable:
  total_deduction
  unless total_deduction > deposit_held
    then deposit_held

rule refund_to_tenant:
  deposit_held - deduction_payable

rule claim_upheld_in_full:
  deduction_payable >= total_claimed


spec renewal_policy 2026-01-01
"""
Whether a renewal offer may be made, and the most that may be asked for the
new term. In force until 2027-01-01: the increase is capped at 4.1% on a
liberalised contract and 2.6% on a regulated one.
Fictional demonstration policy for the HousingAnywhere journey prototype.
Illustrative only: it does not describe HousingAnywhere policy or Dutch law.
"""

uses lemma units

data money: measure
  -> unit eur: 1.00
  -> decimals 2
  -> minimum 0 eur

data current_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What is the tenant paying now?"

data proposed_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What monthly rent is being proposed for the new term?"

data contract_type: text
  -> option "regulated"
  -> option "liberalised"
  -> option "student_housing"
  -> help "What kind of contract is this?"

data notice_given: units.calendar
  -> help "How long before the tenancy ends is the offer being made?"


rule maximum_increase:
  veto "This kind of contract has no renewal cap in the policy"
  unless contract_type is "regulated"   then 2.6%
  unless contract_type is "liberalised" then 4.1%

rule maximum_renewal_rent:
  current_monthly_rent * (100% + maximum_increase)

rule offer_within_cap:
  proposed_monthly_rent <= maximum_renewal_rent

rule notice_is_timely:
  notice_given >= 2 month

rule renewal_offer_permitted:
  offer_within_cap and notice_is_timely


spec renewal_policy 2027-01-01
"""
In force from 2027-01-01: the increase is capped at 2.8% on a liberalised
contract and 1.4% on a regulated one. Everything else carries over unchanged.
Fictional demonstration policy for the HousingAnywhere journey prototype.
Illustrative only: it does not describe HousingAnywhere policy or Dutch law.
"""

uses lemma units

data money: measure
  -> unit eur: 1.00
  -> decimals 2
  -> minimum 0 eur

data current_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What is the tenant paying now?"

data proposed_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What monthly rent is being proposed for the new term?"

data contract_type: text
  -> option "regulated"
  -> option "liberalised"
  -> option "student_housing"
  -> help "What kind of contract is this?"

data notice_given: units.calendar
  -> help "How long before the tenancy ends is the offer being made?"


rule maximum_increase:
  veto "This kind of contract has no renewal cap in the policy"
  unless contract_type is "regulated"   then 1.4%
  unless contract_type is "liberalised" then 2.8%

rule maximum_renewal_rent:
  current_monthly_rent * (100% + maximum_increase)

rule offer_within_cap:
  proposed_monthly_rent <= maximum_renewal_rent

rule notice_is_timely:
  notice_given >= 2 month

rule renewal_offer_permitted:
  offer_within_cap and notice_is_timely


spec shortlist_policy 2026-01-01
"""
In force until 2027-01-01: booking fee 100 eur, deposit capped at one month's
rent, and an approved exception letting the Park Apartment accept five months.
Fictional demonstration policy for the HousingAnywhere shortlist prototype.
Illustrative only: it does not describe HousingAnywhere policy or Dutch law.
Initial payment = first month's rent + deposit + booking fee.
"""

uses lemma units

data money: measure
  -> unit eur: 1.00
  -> decimals 2
  -> minimum 0 eur

data listing_reference: text
  -> help "Which home is being assessed?"

data monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What is the monthly rent for this home?"

data requested_deposit: money
  -> help "What deposit does the advertiser ask for this home?"

data listing_minimum_stay: units.calendar
  -> help "What is the shortest stay this home accepts?"

data intended_stay: units.calendar
  -> help "How long does the tenant intend to stay?"

data maximum_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What is the most the tenant wants to pay per month?"

data maximum_initial_payment: money
  -> help "What is the most the tenant can pay up front?"


rule booking_fee:
  100 eur

rule effective_deposit:
  requested_deposit
  unless requested_deposit > monthly_rent
    then monthly_rent

rule initial_payment:
  monthly_rent + effective_deposit + booking_fee

rule effective_minimum_stay:
  listing_minimum_stay
  unless listing_reference is "C" then 5 month

rule fits_monthly_budget:
  monthly_rent <= maximum_monthly_rent

rule fits_initial_payment_budget:
  initial_payment <= maximum_initial_payment

rule meets_minimum_stay:
  intended_stay >= effective_minimum_stay

rule offer_fits:
  fits_monthly_budget and fits_initial_payment_budget
  and meets_minimum_stay


spec shortlist_policy 2027-01-01
"""
In force from 2027-01-01: the booking fee is abolished. The deposit cap and
the Park Apartment exception carry over unchanged.
Fictional demonstration policy for the HousingAnywhere shortlist prototype.
Illustrative only: it does not describe HousingAnywhere policy or Dutch law.
Initial payment = first month's rent + deposit + booking fee.
"""

uses lemma units

data money: measure
  -> unit eur: 1.00
  -> decimals 2
  -> minimum 0 eur

data listing_reference: text
  -> help "Which home is being assessed?"

data monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What is the monthly rent for this home?"

data requested_deposit: money
  -> help "What deposit does the advertiser ask for this home?"

data listing_minimum_stay: units.calendar
  -> help "What is the shortest stay this home accepts?"

data intended_stay: units.calendar
  -> help "How long does the tenant intend to stay?"

data maximum_monthly_rent: money
  -> help "What is the most the tenant wants to pay per month?"

data maximum_initial_payment: money
  -> help "What is the most the tenant can pay up front?"


rule booking_fee:
  0 eur

rule effective_deposit:
  requested_deposit
  unless requested_deposit > monthly_rent
    then monthly_rent

rule initial_payment:
  monthly_rent + effective_deposit + booking_fee

rule effective_minimum_stay:
  listing_minimum_stay
  unless listing_reference is "C" then 5 month

rule fits_monthly_budget:
  monthly_rent <= maximum_monthly_rent

rule fits_initial_payment_budget:
  initial_payment <= maximum_initial_payment

rule meets_minimum_stay:
  intended_stay >= effective_minimum_stay

rule offer_fits:
  fits_monthly_budget and fits_initial_payment_budget
  and meets_minimum_stay
